<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Terms of Service – <%= botName %></title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wght@12..96,500..800&family=Figtree:wght@400..700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <meta name="description" content="Terms of Service for <%= botName %>, its Discord bot, dashboard and verification pages.">
    <style>
        :root {
            --bg: #0c0a1f;
            --panel: #171337;
            --panel-border: #2a2561;
            --accent: #7c4dff;
            --accent-hover: #a58bff;
            --text: #d6d2f5;
            --text-dim: #8f8abf;
        }
        * { box-sizing: border-box; }
        html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
        body {
            margin: 0;
            background: var(--bg);
            color: var(--text);
            font: 16px/1.7 'Figtree', 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
        }
        .wrap { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 20px 80px; }
        .topnav { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 28px; }
        .topnav a {
            color: var(--text-dim);
            text-decoration: none;
            font-size: 14px;
            padding: 6px 14px;
            border: 1px solid var(--panel-border);
            border-radius: 999px;
        }
        .topnav a:hover { color: var(--text); border-color: var(--accent); }
        .topnav a.active { color: #fff; background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); }
        h1 { font-size: 34px; margin: 0 0 6px; letter-spacing: -0.5px; }
        .updated { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 28px; }
        .card {
            background: var(--panel);
            border: 1px solid var(--panel-border);
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 22px 26px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        .card h2 { font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-dim); margin: 0 0 10px; }
        .card ol { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; columns: 2; column-gap: 32px; }
        .card li { break-inside: avoid; margin: 2px 0; }
        section { margin: 34px 0; scroll-margin-top: 20px; }
        section h2 { font-size: 21px; margin: 0 0 10px; }
        p { margin: 0 0 12px; }
        ul { margin: 0 0 12px; padding-left: 22px; }
        li { margin: 4px 0; }
        a { color: var(--accent-hover); }
        strong { color: #fff; }
        footer { margin-top: 48px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--panel-border); color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 14px; }
        @media (max-width: 600px) { .card ol { columns: 1; } h1 { font-size: 28px; } }
        h1, h2, h3 { font-family: 'Bricolage Grotesque', 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
    :focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #ffc857; outline-offset: 2px; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { * { transition: none !important; scroll-behavior: auto !important; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
    <nav class="topnav">
        <a href="/login"><svg style="vertical-align:-2px;margin-right:6px" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 11l9-8 9 8M5 10v10h5v-6h4v6h5V10"/></svg>Home</a>
        <a href="/support">Support</a>
        <a class="active" href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
    </nav>

    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: <%= updated %></p>

    <p>
        These Terms of Service (“Terms”) apply to <strong><%= botName %></strong> – the Discord bot, the
        web dashboard, the verification and application pages, and the related Discord community
        (together, the “Service”). By using the Service, joining the community, or using the bot’s
        commands, you agree to these Terms. If you don’t agree, please don’t use the Service.
    </p>

    <div class="card">
        <h2>Contents</h2>
        <ol>
            <li><a href="#eligibility">Eligibility</a></li>
            <li><a href="#acceptable-use">Acceptable use</a></li>
            <li><a href="#moderation">Moderation and automated actions</a></li>
            <li><a href="#confessions">Confessions</a></li>
            <li><a href="#verification">Verification</a></li>
            <li><a href="#applications">Staff applications</a></li>
            <li><a href="#dashboard">Dashboard and staff accounts</a></li>
            <li><a href="#ai">AI features</a></li>
            <li><a href="#music">Music</a></li>
            <li><a href="#events">Giveaways, polls and quizzes</a></li>
            <li><a href="#third-parties">Third-party services</a></li>
            <li><a href="#availability">Availability and changes</a></li>
            <li><a href="#termination">Suspension and termination</a></li>
            <li><a href="#disclaimers">Disclaimers and liability</a></li>
            <li><a href="#changes">Changes to these Terms</a></li>
            <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <section id="eligibility">
        <h2>1. Eligibility</h2>
        <p>
            You must meet Discord’s minimum age requirement (13, or higher where your local law says so)
            and comply with the
            <a href="https://discord.com/terms" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Discord Terms of Service</a> and
            <a href="https://discord.com/guidelines" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Community Guidelines</a>.
            Some features, such as staff applications, may have extra requirements that are stated where
            they appear.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="acceptable-use">
        <h2>2. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>When using the Service, you agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>break the server rules, Discord’s Terms or Community Guidelines, or any applicable law;</li>
            <li>harass, threaten, dox, impersonate or discriminate against others;</li>
            <li>post or request illegal, sexually explicit involving minors, or otherwise harmful content;</li>
            <li>spam, raid, or use scripts, self-bots or other automation to abuse commands or the bot;</li>
            <li>evade a ban, mute, timeout or other moderation action, including by using alternate accounts;</li>
            <li>try to bypass verification, CAPTCHA, rate limits or other safeguards;</li>
            <li>probe, attack, scrape or attempt to gain unauthorized access to the bot, dashboard or its data;</li>
            <li>exploit bugs instead of reporting them to staff.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="moderation">
        <h2>3. Moderation and automated actions</h2>
        <p>
            The Service includes moderation tools such as auto-moderation (banned words, spam checks),
            warnings, strikes, timeouts, kicks, bans, timed actions, lockdowns, raid protection,
            ban-evasion flags and an impersonation guard. Some of these act automatically.
        </p>
        <p>
            Moderation actions are recorded as cases and are visible to staff. Automated systems can make
            mistakes. A flag or automatic action is a prompt for staff review, not a final judgment about you.
            Staff have discretion over what is and isn’t acceptable and over the action taken. If you think
            an action was a mistake, contact staff (see <a href="#contact">Contact</a>) and we’ll take another look.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="confessions">
        <h2>4. Confessions</h2>
        <p>
            Confessions are posted publicly without your name. They are <strong>not anonymous to
            staff</strong>: the author’s Discord account is recorded in a private staff channel so that
            abuse can be dealt with. Confessions must follow the acceptable use rules above. Staff may delete
            confessions and may remove access to the confession feature from anyone who abuses it.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="verification">
        <h2>5. Verification</h2>
        <p>
            Some areas require you to verify on our website. Verification asks you to sign in with Discord,
            complete a CAPTCHA, and confirm that you agree to the rules. Successful verification grants a
            role in the server. It doesn’t entitle you to any particular access or privilege, and it can be
            reviewed or revoked.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="applications">
        <h2>6. Staff applications</h2>
        <p>
            If you apply for a moderator or co-owner position, you agree that your answers are true and may
            be read by the server’s ownership and staff team. Submitting an application doesn’t guarantee a
            response or a position, and decisions on applications are at the owners’ discretion.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="dashboard">
        <h2>7. Dashboard and staff accounts</h2>
        <p>
            The dashboard is for authorized staff. Access is tied to your rank and may be limited by
            settings such as IP allowlists. Keep your credentials private, don’t share your session or
            account, and only use the tools you’re permitted to use. Actions taken on the dashboard may be
            logged. Access can be removed at any time.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="ai">
        <h2>8. AI features</h2>
        <p>
            Some features use AI-generated text. AI responses can be wrong, odd or inappropriate, and are
            provided for convenience and entertainment, not as professional, legal, medical or financial
            advice. “Nerd Mode” is only used for the April Fools update. Don’t put sensitive personal information into AI features. Text you submit to them (or
            that triggers them) is sent to the third-party providers described in the
            <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="music">
        <h2>9. Music</h2>
        <p>
            The music feature plays audio from third-party sources in voice channels based on what members
            request. We don’t host that content. You’re responsible for what you request and for
            following the rules of the platforms it comes from. Music features may be removed or changed if a
            source stops allowing them.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="events">
        <h2>10. Giveaways, polls and quizzes</h2>
        <p>
            Giveaways, polls, quizzes and similar features are for fun. Hosts may set their own conditions,
            disqualify entries that break the rules, and re-draw winners. These features are not sponsored,
            endorsed or administered by Discord.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="third-parties">
        <h2>11. Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
            The Service relies on third parties such as Discord and the providers listed in the
            <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. Your use of those services is governed by their own terms,
            and we’re not responsible for them.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="availability">
        <h2>12. Availability and changes</h2>
        <p>
            The Service is provided as a community project. It may go offline for maintenance or because
            of outages, and features may be added, changed or removed at any time without notice. We don’t
            promise that it will be uninterrupted or error-free.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="termination">
        <h2>13. Suspension and termination</h2>
        <p>
            We may warn, restrict, suspend or remove your access to the Service or the community at any
            time, particularly if you break these Terms or the server rules. You can stop using the Service
            whenever you like by leaving the server and, if you used the website, revoking the app in your
            Discord settings under Authorized Apps. Records we hold about you, such as moderation history, are kept after you leave, are
            removed from the server, or your Discord account is banned; see the <a href="/privacy#retention">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="disclaimers">
        <h2>14. Disclaimers and liability</h2>
        <p>
            The Service is provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any kind, to the
            fullest extent permitted by law. To the fullest extent permitted by law, the operators and staff
            of <%= botName %> are not liable for any indirect, incidental or consequential damages, or for any
            loss of data, accounts, roles or content, arising from your use of the Service. Nothing in these
            Terms limits any rights you have that can’t be limited by law.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="changes">
        <h2>15. Changes to these Terms</h2>
        <p>
            We may update these Terms from time to time. The “Last updated” date above shows when they last
            changed. If you keep using the Service after an update, you accept the new Terms. For significant
            changes we’ll try to give notice in the community.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
        <h2>16. Contact</h2>
        <p>
            Questions, appeals or concerns about these Terms? Reach the staff team
            <% if (supportUrl) { %>through our <a href="<%= supportUrl %>" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Discord server</a><% } else { %>through the Discord server or by direct-messaging the bot (your message is relayed to staff)<% } %><% if (contactEmail) { %>
            or by email at <a href="mailto:<%= contactEmail %>"><%= contactEmail %></a><% } %>.
        </p>
    </section>

    <footer>
        <a href="/support">Support</a> · <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> · <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
        <br>
        <%= botName %> is an independent community project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Discord Inc.
    </footer>
</div>
</body>
</html>
